        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "I think I found a way to handle nicely all possible `listchar`s combinations (and `indent-blankline.nvim`). The idea is to support an `''` value, in which case prefix won't be prepended, but rather `virt_text_win_col` increased to the proper amount. That way prefix will be 'transparent' and will not overwrite any `listchar`s.\r\n\r\nHere how it looks with `prefix = ''` and `vim.o.listchars = 'leadmultispace:*-'`:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"483\" alt=\"leading\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/5783792/202011214-53f43cd5-7aec-4583-bc2e-52d9d00611c0.png\">\r\n\r\nI've updated PR and added a remark about empty string value case handling in the documentation. Tested on Neovim 0.8.\r\n",
